-## Persistence blockers to resolve before integration
-
-Source review found the following inherited behavior. Configuration tests stub
-the storage layer and do not claim these paths work:
-
-- `wsclient/wsclient.js` starts cleanup/keepalive timers on every reconnect but
-  does not cancel them on close. The cleanup callback loses its interval value.
-- The same file shares initialization metadata and block/time fields across
-  nodes, reads `myData.data.id` without checking the envelope, and does not request
-  the initial viewer snapshot or handle Primus heartbeats explicitly.
-- Its startup call to `Populate.initDbAndTables()` deletes charts, then refers
-  to an undefined `record`; the caller does not await or catch that initialization.
-- `db_methods/populate.js` interpolates node report values into several SQL
-  statements. Use parameterized statements and verify ordinary quoted text
-  survives round trips before enabling persistence.
-- `POSTGRESQL_Setup.sh` starts by dropping a database, does not switch its
